{"duration_api_ms":297053,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"49487f52-5f9a-4f79-9d3d-4e40bc94175a","total_cost_usd":0.338454,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12470,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":28857,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":22078},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12470,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":28857,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12470,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12470},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":28857,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":12470,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.338454,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":22078,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"No feasible design exists yet. 10 of 20 evaluations failed on geometry and none of the 10 valid ones is feasible. The geometry failures fit a closed-form rule: the fore-cone length is (R - Rs(1-cos t) - Rn cos t)/tan t, with Rn = bluntness*D and Rs = 0.1*D. This is equivalent to (bluntness - 0.1)*cos(cone_half_angle) <= 0.4, independent of D. I reproduced the reported negative lengths of -48.9 mm (C-0e7ec9742f84) and -22.8 mm (C-2e989122c857), and it separates every valid row from every invalid row. I keep this quantity <= ~0.38 in every proposal. The limits implied by the margins are max_g 12.0 and bondline 450 K. Heatshield mass fraction scales roughly as 0.09*D^2 in units of its limit, which puts D at about 3.3 or below. Max_g is mainly set by flight-path angle, so gamma should be about -3.0 to -3.8 deg. On the valid points, flux falls with larger D and larger bluntness, and bondline temperature falls with larger D, steeper gamma and larger bluntness. So I target D ~3.0-3.3, high bluntness, cone angle 60-70 deg and gamma ~-3.5 deg.\",\"evidence\":[\"Geometry rule check: C-cf5ade290acc (b=1.076, cone 33.9) gives 0.98*0.83=0.81 > 0.4, invalid. C-63aaa0985529 (b=0.523, cone 29.7) gives 0.37 <= 0.4, valid. C-7fd3f4505944 (0.65*0.80=0.52) is invalid and C-f97dae207371 (0.26) is valid. All 20 rows are consistent.\",\"Max_g limit is 12.0: C-50a0a474d0f6 has 12.059 with margin -0.0049. The limit for bondline temperature is 450 K, from C-ee99f55de428 (455.54 with margin -0.0123).\",\"Max_g vs gamma: 9.4 g at -1.85 (C-f97dae207371), 10.2 g at -2.64 (C-ee99f55de428), 12.5 g at -4.10 (C-63aaa0985529), 13.1 g at -4.26 (C-ab9827dc6929), 16.2-17.2 g at about -6 (C-baa2f9e65f32, C-26bc5a06b4e4, C-12010dd082dd). Small D looks slightly worse: C-50a0a474d0f6 reaches 12.06 g at only -3.1 deg. I therefore stay at gamma >= -3.9.\",\"Mass fraction divided by D^2 is about 0.089-0.091 for cone >= 62 (C-36f9165b9496, C-baa2f9e65f32, C-c72c38c9187a, C-12010dd082dd), 0.097-0.101 for cone 42-53, and 0.11 for cone 30-38 (C-63aaa0985529, C-f97dae207371). The margin is 0.028 at D=2.985 with cone 29.7 and -0.004 at D=3.21 with cone 52.8, so high cone angle allows a larger D.\",\"Bondline temperature fit on the valid rows: T-300 ~ 103*(D/3.21)^-0.8*(sin|gamma|/0.0743)^-0.4*(b/0.399)^-0.2, anchored on C-ab9827dc6929. It reproduces C-f97dae207371 (444.7), C-36f9165b9496 (398), C-26bc5a06b4e4 (373) and C-baa2f9e65f32 (373.6) to within a few K.\",\"Flux fit anchored on C-ab9827dc6929 (479 kW/m2): q ~ 479k*(D/3.21)^-1.5*(b/0.399)^-0.5*(sin|gamma|/0.0743)^0.3. It matches C-26bc5a06b4e4, C-baa2f9e65f32 and C-c72c38c9187a within ~10%. C-63aaa0985529 (cone 29.7) is ~15% above the fit, which suggests small cone angles raise flux.\",\"C-36f9165b9496 (b=0.87, cone 65) has the lowest bondline temperature of the mid-size designs (398 K at D=2.55) and fails only max_g (gamma -4.86). Raising D to ~3.1 and easing gamma to ~-3.6 should make it feasible.\"],\"mechanism\":\"Peak heating falls as ballistic coefficient falls (larger D, higher drag from a blunter and wider cone) and as nose radius grows. Bondline temperature follows the integrated heat load, which is lower for steeper entry and higher for shallow entry, where the soak time is long. Peak deceleration is set mainly by entry angle, so shallow gamma protects max_g but raises bondline temperature. The best compromise is the largest D the mass-fraction limit allows, high bluntness with a cone wide enough to keep the geometry valid, and gamma of about -3.5 deg. High cone angle also reduces heatshield area, which buys diameter.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The scalings are my own fits to only 10 valid points, plus a physics prior for exponents. The bluntness effect beyond b=0.87 is extrapolated, since no valid point has b above 0.87. The g dependence on D and cone is poorly constrained. The mass-fraction limit near D=3.3 rests on a ~0.089*D^2 fit. The flux dependence on cone angle is only hinted at by C-63aaa0985529.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-36f9165b9496\",\"rationale\":\"Enlarge D to 3.1 and ease gamma to -3.6 on the low-temperature, high-bluntness design to fix max_g. Expect f_mass ~0.86 of its limit.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.1,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":335000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":399,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Most likely first feasible design; it anchors the fits in the target region.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-36f9165b9496\",\"rationale\":\"Slightly larger D=3.2 with shallower gamma -3.4, for a lower g margin risk and lower flux.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":310000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":397,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests whether D=3.2 still meets the mass-fraction limit at cone 65.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-36f9165b9496\",\"rationale\":\"Smaller D=3.0 with steeper gamma -3.75 to probe the max_g limit while keeping mass margin.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.75},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":352000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":398,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Locates the g boundary in gamma at D=3.0.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-36f9165b9496\",\"rationale\":\"Push bluntness to 1.1 with cone 70 (geometry value 0.342) to test whether higher bluntness lowers both objectives.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.1,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.1,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":300000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":396,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Extrapolates bluntness beyond the observed range; a large potential gain in the hypervolume.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-36f9165b9496\",\"rationale\":\"Bluntness 1.15 with cone 70 (geometry value 0.359) at D=3.1, gamma -3.5. This is the upper bluntness probe.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.1,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.15,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":295000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":395,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the diminishing-return limit of bluntness and the safety of the geometry rule near its edge.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ab9827dc6929\",\"rationale\":\"Moderate bluntness 0.7 with cone 58 at D=3.1, gamma -3.5. Cone 58 is safe (geometry value 0.318) and reduces area versus cone 52.8.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.1,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.7,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":58.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":370000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":404,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Interpolates the bluntness trend between 0.4 and 0.87 at a fixed feasible-looking D and gamma.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ab9827dc6929\",\"rationale\":\"Bluntness 0.5 with cone 55 at D=3.1, gamma -3.5; a lower-bluntness anchor for the b trend.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.1,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.5,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":55.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":430000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":410,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Separates the effect of bluntness from D and gamma in the fits.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ab9827dc6929\",\"rationale\":\"Bluntness 0.6 with cone 60 at D=3.2, gamma -3.3. This design has a shallower gamma and a larger D.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.6,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":60.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":365000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":406,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks the mass fraction at D=3.2 with cone 60 and measures a gamma-shallow point.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-36f9165b9496\",\"rationale\":\"Shallow gamma -3.0 at D=3.2 to bracket the trade-off, with lower flux and higher temperature and a comfortable g margin.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":295000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":402,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Extends the front toward low flux and confirms the gamma trend of bondline temperature.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-36f9165b9496\",\"rationale\":\"Steeper gamma -3.9 at D=3.1 to probe the g limit near 12 g while reducing bondline temperature.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.1,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.9},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":335000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":395,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Finds the steep-gamma edge of the feasible region; the g margin is about 0-5%.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-36f9165b9496\",\"rationale\":\"Larger D=3.3 with cone 68 and gamma -3.5 to probe the mass-fraction limit (expected ~0.96 of the limit).\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":68.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":295000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":394,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Locates the D ceiling for high-cone designs, which decides how far flux and temperature can drop.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-36f9165b9496\",\"rationale\":\"D=3.35 with b=1.0 and cone 70 (geometry value 0.308) as a deliberate upper-D probe on mass fraction.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.35,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.0,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":280000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":390,\"feasible\":false},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Its mass margin is estimated at ~0.01 and could go either way; the result pins down the mass-fraction limit.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-36f9165b9496\",\"rationale\":\"Bluntness 0.7 with cone 66 at D=3.25, gamma -3.5, testing a lower-bluntness large-D combination.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.25,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.7,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":66.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":340000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":400,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Adds a second data point on mass fraction at D~3.25.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ab9827dc6929\",\"rationale\":\"Bluntness 0.8, cone 62 (geometry value 0.329), D=3.0, gamma -3.6. This is a safe mid-range design with a large mass margin.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.0,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.8,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":62.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":360000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":402,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"A robust feasible candidate to secure hypervolume early.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-63aaa0985529\",\"rationale\":\"Smaller D=2.9 with b=0.87, cone 65 and gamma -3.7, a conservative design with a large mass margin.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":2.9,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.87,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":65.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.7},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":365000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":402,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests how much D matters at fixed b, cone and gamma by comparison with proposals at D=3.1-3.2.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-36f9165b9496\",\"rationale\":\"Bluntness 1.0 with cone 67 (geometry value 0.352) at D=3.15, gamma -3.4.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.15,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.0,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":67.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":300000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":397,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Intermediate step between b=0.87 and b=1.1-1.15 for the bluntness trend.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-36f9165b9496\",\"rationale\":\"Reduce cone to 61 (geometry value 0.373) at b=0.87, D=3.1, gamma -3.6, to isolate the cone-angle effect against the cone-65 proposal.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.1,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":61.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":345000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":399,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"A controlled comparison of cone angle: the same D, b and gamma as another proposal.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ab9827dc6929\",\"rationale\":\"D=3.2, b=0.87, cone 65, gamma -3.7. This is a steeper-gamma variant at larger D, to test g and mass together.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.87,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":65.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.7},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":322000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":395,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Candidate for the lowest bondline temperature that still satisfies max_g.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-63aaa0985529\",\"rationale\":\"Low cone 40 with b=0.5 (geometry value 0.306) at D=2.9, gamma -3.5, to measure the cone-angle effect on flux, mass fraction and g.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":2.9,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.5,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":40.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":520000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":417,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Discriminates the cone-angle effect visible in C-63aaa0985529 and C-f97dae207371; this exploration is likely dominated.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-36f9165b9496\",\"rationale\":\"b=1.0 with cone 70 at D=3.0 and shallow gamma -3.2. A high-bluntness design with a large g margin and lower flux.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.0,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.0,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.2},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":315000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":402,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Extends the front at the shallow-gamma end with high bluntness.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0}]}","ttft_ms":243316,"type":"result","duration_ms":297104,"uuid":"7da133cd-4209-4597-9d36-d326a9d24b11","ttft_stream_ms":1078,"time_to_request_ms":49,"first_content_frame_ms":1078,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
